{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if the jubilee be.</b> From here Rabbi Yehudah would say: the jubilee is destined to cease (Torat Kohanim Leviticus 2)." "<b>And if the jubilee be.</b> That is to say, this is not a sale that reverts in the jubilee, for an inheritance does not revert — even if the jubilee comes, the inheritance does not return to his tribe. And so it turns out that it is added <b>to the inheritance of the tribe that shall be theirs.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:57.121136679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}